# ---- Unity generated -------------------------------------------------------
# Library and Temp are rebuilt from Assets + ProjectSettings on first open. They
# are also the largest folders here (446 MB) and would make the repo unusable.
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Never commit an IDE's generated project files -- they embed absolute paths
# from whoever last opened the project.
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Crash reports and asset-import noise
sysinfo.txt
*.stackdump
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# ---- This project ----------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered-art backups and retired assets: 183 MB of history that the game does
# not need to build. _char_dark_backup holds the RAW Blender renders that
# Tools/brighten_chars.py processes into Assets/. Losing it does not break the
# build (the processed art is committed) but it does mean brighten_chars.py
# cannot re-run until you re-render -- the script detects this and refuses
# rather than double-applying its LUT to already-brightened art.
Tools/_char_dark_backup/
Tools/_unused_assets/
Tools/_pre3d_art_backup/
Tools/_painterly_food_backup/
Tools/_painterly_object_backup/
Tools/_placeholder_anim_backup/
Tools/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Diagnostic renders written by the Blender probe scripts
_probe_out/
_CharacterPreview/

# ---- Credentials: nothing here should ever exist, but be explicit ----------
# Rushhouse has no backend and no keys. These patterns are a tripwire so that a
# future addition (Supabase, Firebase, a signing key) cannot be committed by
# reflex. Real values belong in GitHub Secrets, never in the tree.
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.cer
*.mobileprovision
*.keystore
*.jks
.env
.env.*
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
secrets.json
**/ServiceAccount*.json

# The Xcode project tarball handed to CI via a GitHub Release. ~256 MB, which is
# over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so committing it does not fail quietly --
# it fails the whole push. It is a build output; it belongs on a Release, not here.
xcode-project.tar.gz
# Batch-mode Unity logs written next to the project by the build commands.
unity_*.log
